  "worked_solution": "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $15$ | $-13$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $10$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 1 & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -13 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.",
